        "The days at Chitrakuta had settled into a quiet rhythm. The mountain stood beneath the changing light of the seasons, its slopes covered with trees, flowering creepers, and patches of open ground where sunlight reached the forest floor. Nearby streams carried clear water through the rocks, while birds moved freely between the branches. Away from the ceremonies and responsibilities of Ayodhya, Rama, Sita, and Lakshmana had made a simple dwelling their home.",
